1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:11,852
I am the adversary, the sceptical reviewer. I try to break your result before a referee does: I re-run your analysis and I check what your write-up claims.

2
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:29,511
I re-run your code rather than trusting the write-up. Most of what I see is not a classifier: it is a t-test, an analysis of variance, a regression, a survival curve, the statistics of an ordinary thesis. I reproduce those the same way.

3
00:00:29,511 --> 00:00:43,661
I look for the classic faults: the wrong test for the data, a hidden grouping, samples that are not independent, a result that seems too good, and, for a prediction model, test data leaking into training.

4
00:00:43,661 --> 00:01:00,246
In a write-up, I check that each cited paper is real and says what you claim. For a prediction model, I go through the reporting checklist a journal will use, TRIPOD plus AI, and name each item you missed.

5
00:01:00,649 --> 00:01:10,852
My scope is how a result was produced and whether it holds up. Each finding is marked as checked, when I confirmed it by running something, or only suspected.

6
00:01:10,852 --> 00:01:24,280
When a result touches a patent or governed data, I refer it to the lawyer myself, mid-audit, and fold their verdict into mine. I audit what was built; I do not build it.

7
00:01:24,700 --> 00:01:34,252
A real run, on the example paper that ships with Murmurent: do colonies grown in serum come out larger, and does the difference hold?

8
00:01:34,252 --> 00:01:54,803
The verdict is Questions. The number reproduces exactly, but the serum and control samples come from different countries, the test is one-sided and the write-up does not say so, and the Methods misdescribe the code. Each finding says whether I checked it or only suspect it.

9
00:01:55,200 --> 00:02:04,427
Say what to audit: the tests in a thesis chapter, a classifier before submission, or a Results section against its own numbers.

10
00:02:04,427 --> 00:02:12,342
Say what you want settled, and I say for each finding whether I checked it or only suspect it.

11
00:02:12,750 --> 00:02:26,481
To use me, type to Claude Code and name me: ask the adversary to audit the statistics in a chapter, or a result before you submit it. Give me the folder with the code and the data.

12
00:02:26,481 --> 00:02:39,787
The first line is my verdict: Pass, Questions or Reject. Then each finding, marked checked or suspected, with what would settle it.
